{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjEsPpr86jFBPPtqP4Fp","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01E5C8MLtFKC25uFZEbLHFNL","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-215625__x13c81f/work/PLAN.md","offset":205,"limit":135},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6605,"cache_read_input_tokens":329908,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6605},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9db0da04-284f-40b5-8e80-2e3f7ed2ab1c","uuid":"3b5328aa-668e-4c41-b0da-0cce921eab4a","timestamp":"2026-11-05T05:37:07.377Z","request_id":"req_011CgjEsPXFEHQoZ7RDNFKJb","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01E5C8MLtFKC25uFZEbLHFNL":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-215625__x13c81f/work/PLAN.md","offset":205,"limit":135}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01E5C8MLtFKC25uFZEbLHFNL","type":"tool_result","content":"205\t\n206\t**Split screen (tested).** Build `inkView(scene, camA, vec2(screenUV.x.mul(2), screenUV.y), 2)` and `inkView(scene, camB, vec2(screenUV.x.sub(0.5).mul(2), screenUV.y), 2)`, give both cameras aspect `(w/2)/h`, and composite with `mix(b.node, a.node, step(screenUV.x, 0.5))` plus a 6 px ink bar at the seam. Rebuild `post.outputNode` and set `post.needsUpdate = true` when entering or leaving split, so the second pass only runs when needed.\n207\t\n208\t### 2.6 Rapier\n209\t\n210\t- **Queries see nothing until the first `world.step()`.** Step once after building a zone, before baking nav.\n211\t- **Terrain:** a trimesh from the same vertices as the visible mesh (`ColliderDesc.trimesh(new Float32Array(pos.array), new Uint32Array(index.array))`) matches to 2 µm. Heightfield index order is easy to get wrong; skip it.\n212\t- **Actors:** kinematic position-based body, capsule collider, one `world.createCharacterController(0.02)` each: `setUp({x:0,y:1,z:0})`, `setMaxSlopeClimbAngle` (50°, in radians), `enableSnapToGround(0.35)`, `enableAutostep(0.4,0.2,false)`, `setSlideEnabled(true)`. Feed the delta to `computeColliderMovement(collider, delta, QueryFilterFlags.EXCLUDE_SENSORS, filterGroups)`, then `setNextKinematicTranslation(p + computedMovement())`.\n213\t- **Rays and shape casts hit sensors** unless you pass `QueryFilterFlags.EXCLUDE_SENSORS`.\n214\t- **Collision groups** are `(membership << 16) | filter`, on colliders and as `filterGroups`. This table is the plan's design; only the ragdoll's group value was run:\n215\t\n216\t| Group | Bit | Collides with |\n217\t|---|---|---|\n218\t| STATIC | 1 | everything |\n219\t| PLAYER | 2 | static, prop, enemy |\n220\t| ENEMY | 4 | static, prop, player (not other enemies: crowds separate by steering, otherwise they jam) |\n221\t| PROP | 8 | static, player, enemy, prop, ragdoll |\n222\t| RAGDOLL | 16 | static, prop |\n223\t| SENSOR | 32 | none (triggers use your own box tests) |\n224\t\n225\t- **Ragdoll:** capsule bodies with `RAPIER.JointData.spherical(anchorA, anchorB)` via `world.createImpulseJoint`, `setAngularDamping(0.6)`. Stable in test.\n226\t- **Budget:** 60 character controllers, 30 dynamic bodies, a 29k-triangle trimesh and 8 rays cost ~6 ms per step, so the sim runs ~170 steps/s with no renderer. That is why tests skip rendering (§15).\n227\t\n228\t### 2.7 AI Hub: what passes\n229\t\n230\tFetch once with `curl -fsSO` into `hub/`, from `https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/`: `session.js`, `harness.html`, `bridge.js`, `round.js`, `README.md`, `examples/arena.html`. Read the README: it is the contract. This skeleton passed every harness scenario with a heavy WebGPU scene in every copy (2 and 4 players on a poor network, host leaving, server copy):\n231\t\n232\t```js\n233\tconst info = await AIHub.connect({ mode:'shared-world', seats:[1,4], card:true });\n234\tif (!info) return startStandalone();             // not in a session: title screen, attract, everything\n235\t// A session opens straight into the round: no title, menus or prompts other than the card.\n236\taddEventListener('keydown', e => { if (e.key === 'Enter') AIHub.answer('ready'); });\n237\tAIHub.on('card', c => drawCard(c));\n238\tif (!info.server) startRendererInBackground();   // never block ready() on shaders; a server copy never renders\n239\tbuildSimAndArena();\n240\tAIHub.ready();                                   // once, no key press\n241\tAIHub.on('start', () => unlockAudio());\n242\tAIHub.on('message', (data, from) => net.receive(data, from));\n243\tAIHub.on('leave', ({ id }) => sim.dropPlayer(id));\n244\tAIHub.on('time-up', () => { if (AIHub.isHost) finishRound(); });   // at once, in the handler: graceMs is 5 s\n245\tAIHub.on('end', ({ reason }) => endRound(reason));                  // stop input, sends and sound; hub shows results\n246\tsetInterval(pumpSimAndNet, 50);                  // a timer, not rAF: four software-rendered copies crawl\n247\t// Play begins when AIHub.time() >= 0; draw the countdown before that.\n248\t```\n249\t\n250\tDetails that fail the check if missed:\n251\t\n252\t- The pasted client must be byte-exact and appear **once**. For client 1.4.0, SHA-256 from `/*! aihub-session ` through its last line (LF endings) is `529eac78c54cfff0e60d375a9c63f66d1a594327ddcc262a2bdf9b1f2fb6582a`. Never put the banner text anywhere else in the page.\n253\t- Any `[AIHub]` console warning fails, so never exceed 20 sends/s (burst 40) or 16 KB. Keep your own token bucket at 18/s and keep unreliable messages under 1,100 bytes.\n254\t- No `alert`, `confirm`, `prompt`, `window.open`, sockets, navigation or external `fetch`. Catch every promise (`requestPointerLock()`, `requestFullscreen()`, `playEffect()`, `audio.resume()`): an unhandled rejection counts as an error.\n255\t- The harness pokes synthetic keys with `code:'w'`, not `KeyW`. Map by `e.code`, falling back to `e.key`.\n256\t- On its own the game must draw and survive Enter/Space presses with no errors, and must leave `Math.random` alone. A DOM title over the canvas guarantees the \"drawn\" check even if WebGPU is unavailable.\n257\t- In a session `localStorage` is an empty in-memory copy, so never depend on saved data there. Hub names are text: `textContent` only.\n258\t- `Create + Options` belongs to the hub: ignore Options while Create is held.\n259\t\n260\tRun it like the hub does. Serve your dev folder from Node (`server.listen(0,'127.0.0.1')`), open with the five flags plus `--no-sandbox --autoplay-policy=no-user-gesture-required`, viewport 1280×860:\n261\t\n262\t```\n263\t/hub/harness.html?game=/dist/game.html&players=N&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1&scenario=S&play=8000\n264\t```\n265\t\n266\tWait for `body[data-complete=\"true\"]`, then require `window.__hubCheck.pass`. Scenarios: `players=2,3,4` with `standard`, `players=3` with `host-leave`, `players=2` with `server`. Each took 10–15 s here.\n267\t\n268\t---\n269\t\n270\t## 3. Architecture\n271\t\n272\t```\n273\ttools/build.mjs  tools/test.mjs\n274\thub/             session client, harness (fetched, unedited)\n275\tdocs/CONTENT.md  how to add a zone, enemy, weapon, item, script command (the designer's manual)\n276\tSTATUS.md        your own progress notes, so a context reset costs nothing\n277\tsrc/main.js      boot: session / standalone / test modes\n278\tsrc/core/        loop, rng, events, tunables, save, coverage\n279\tsrc/input/       action map, gamepad, keyboard+mouse, device tracking, virtual pads, bot injection\n280\tsrc/phys/        Rapier wrapper: statics from pieces, character controllers, queries, ragdolls, debris\n281\tsrc/sim/         player, weapons, damage, enemies + AI, nav, partner, director, inventory, shop, qte, script runner, triggers, bosses, siege, chapter flow\n282\tsrc/content/     DATA ONLY: identity, weapons, items, enemies, shop stock, tunable defaults, zones/*, dialogue, documents, music patterns\n283\tsrc/art/         palette, toon materials, prefab kit, character builder + outfits, weapon models, clip library, FX\n284\tsrc/render/      renderer start, ink, light pool, camera rig, split screen, view sync\n285\tsrc/audio/       engine and buses, reverb, sfx recipes, voice, music\n286\tsrc/ui/          focus engine, glyphs, HUD, all screens, comic cutscene overlay\n287\tsrc/net/         hub session flow, snapshot codec, rate limiter\n288\tsrc/bot/         one brain shared by attract mode and the playthrough test\n289\ttests/\n290\t```\n291\t\n292\t**Sim and view are separate.** `src/sim` never touches the renderer, the DOM or audio. It owns state and may own CPU-only `Bone` hierarchies, because hit zones and mixers run there. It emits events on a bus; view, audio, UI and net subscribe. `?test=1&norender=1` runs the same code with no renderer at all, stepped by hand.\n293\t\n294\t**The sim is an object you can create and throw away,** with no module-level state: attract mode, retries and tests each make their own. On zone change call `world.free()` and dispose the old geometries and materials, so attract can loop for hours without running out of memory.\n295\t\n296\t**Loop.** Fixed 60 Hz:\n297\t\n298\t```js\n299\tacc = min(acc + realDt * timeScale, 0.25); while (acc >= STEP) { sim.step(STEP); acc -= STEP; }\n300\t```\n301\t\n302\t- `timeScale` handles hit-stop and slow motion by changing the step count; `dt` is never varied.\n303\t- Rendering uses `renderer.setAnimationLoop`.\n304\t- In a session a 50 ms `setInterval` also pumps the sim and net. A server copy has only the timer.\n305\t- Standalone pauses on `visibilitychange`; sessions never pause.\n306\t\n307\t**Determinism.** All sim randomness comes from seeded streams in `core/rng.js` (from `AIHub.rng('siege')` in a session). `Math.random`, `Date.now` and `performance.now` are banned in `src/sim`, and a test greps for them. Visual-only randomness uses a separate cosmetic stream.\n308\t\n309\t**Tunables.** `tunables.define('enemy.hpMult', { label, min, max, step, def, group })`. Gameplay reads `T.enemy.hpMult` every time and never caches it, so dev sliders apply live. Defaults live in `src/content/tunables.js`.\n310\t\n311\t**Content is data.** So the rest of the game can be built later with ordinary tools, every zone, enemy, weapon, item, shop list, dialogue line and script is plain JSON-able data, documented in `docs/CONTENT.md`. A zone:\n312\t\n313\t```js\n314\t{ id:'ch1.lane', title:'Hive Lane', palette:'dusk', music:'explore', reverb:'outdoor', size:[30,120],\n315\t  terrain:{ seed:11, bumps:0.4, path:[[15,0],[14,60],[16,120]] },\n316\t  pieces:[ {kit:'fence',at:[4,0,10],ry:0,len:30}, {kit:'farmhouse',at:[24,0,40],ry:-90,windows:['vault']} ],\n317\t  lights:[ {kind:'lantern',at:[12,3,30]} ],\n318\t  entry:{at:[15,0,2],ry:0}, exits:[ {to:'ch1.square',box:[10,0,118,20,3,120]} ],\n319\t  spawns:[ {id:'e1',type:'sweetened',gear:'pitchfork',at:[14,0,40],wake:'seen'} ],\n320\t  pickups:[ {item:'ammo9',n:15,at:[22,1,38],in:'crate'} ],\n321\t  triggers:[ {box:[10,0,30,20,3,34],once:true,run:'ambush'} ],\n322\t  scripts:{ ambush:[ ['say','dash','Friendly town.'], ['wake','e1'], ['music','tension'] ] },\n323\t  bot:[ ['go',[15,50]], ['fight'], ['go',[15,118]] ] }\n324\t```\n325\t\n326\tScript commands, the single language for level events and cutscenes: `say radio cam anim move wait wake spawn give flag if music sfx qte letterbox panel fade objective gate save chapterEnd`. Dev mode can copy the current zone as JSON and load a zone JSON dropped on the window.\n327\t\n328\t**Nav.** At zone load (after one `world.step()`), rasterise a 0.5 m walkable grid with down-rays and capsule overlap tests, with an 8-neighbour step-height check. `flowTo(target)` is a Dijkstra flow field, cached per target cell and refreshed at 4 Hz. Enemies, Winnie and the bot all use it, adding separation steering for crowds. Ladders, windows and gaps are explicit links that carry the action to play.\n329\t\n330\t**Hits.** Bullets ray-cast statics with `EXCLUDE_SENSORS` to get a stopping distance, then test ray against analytic capsules built from bone world positions (head sphere, torso, 2 arms, 2 legs). Deterministic, precise and independent of the renderer.\n331\t\n332\t**Test hook.** `window.__GAME`:\n333\t\n334\t- `state()`: mode, screen, chapter, zone, objective, cutscene, qte, focus, last device, player hp/ammo/weapon/pos, enemy count, partner, money, backend, `deviceLost`, `gpuErrors`, audio gains, coverage.\n335\t- `step(n)` and `input(padState)`.\n336\t- `teleport`, `setFlag`, `goZone`.\n337\t\n338\t---\n339\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9db0da04-284f-40b5-8e80-2e3f7ed2ab1c","uuid":"2e80ecb5-3a01-43fd-89ff-df2d2bfa662a","timestamp":"2026-11-05T05:37:07.383Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-215625__x13c81f/work/PLAN.md","content":"\n**Split screen (tested).** Build `inkView(scene, camA, vec2(screenUV.x.mul(2), screenUV.y), 2)` and `inkView(scene, camB, vec2(screenUV.x.sub(0.5).mul(2), screenUV.y), 2)`, give both cameras aspect `(w/2)/h`, and composite with `mix(b.node, a.node, step(screenUV.x, 0.5))` plus a 6 px ink bar at the seam. Rebuild `post.outputNode` and set `post.needsUpdate = true` when entering or leaving split, so the second pass only runs when needed.\n\n### 2.6 Rapier\n\n- **Queries see nothing until the first `world.step()`.** Step once after building a zone, before baking nav.\n- **Terrain:** a trimesh from the same vertices as the visible mesh (`ColliderDesc.trimesh(new Float32Array(pos.array), new Uint32Array(index.array))`) matches to 2 µm. Heightfield index order is easy to get wrong; skip it.\n- **Actors:** kinematic position-based body, capsule collider, one `world.createCharacterController(0.02)` each: `setUp({x:0,y:1,z:0})`, `setMaxSlopeClimbAngle` (50°, in radians), `enableSnapToGround(0.35)`, `enableAutostep(0.4,0.2,false)`, `setSlideEnabled(true)`. Feed the delta to `computeColliderMovement(collider, delta, QueryFilterFlags.EXCLUDE_SENSORS, filterGroups)`, then `setNextKinematicTranslation(p + computedMovement())`.\n- **Rays and shape casts hit sensors** unless you pass `QueryFilterFlags.EXCLUDE_SENSORS`.\n- **Collision groups** are `(membership << 16) | filter`, on colliders and as `filterGroups`. This table is the plan's design; only the ragdoll's group value was run:\n\n| Group | Bit | Collides with |\n|---|---|---|\n| STATIC | 1 | everything |\n| PLAYER | 2 | static, prop, enemy |\n| ENEMY | 4 | static, prop, player (not other enemies: crowds separate by steering, otherwise they jam) |\n| PROP | 8 | static, player, enemy, prop, ragdoll |\n| RAGDOLL | 16 | static, prop |\n| SENSOR | 32 | none (triggers use your own box tests) |\n\n- **Ragdoll:** capsule bodies with `RAPIER.JointData.spherical(anchorA, anchorB)` via `world.createImpulseJoint`, `setAngularDamping(0.6)`. Stable in test.\n- **Budget:** 60 character controllers, 30 dynamic bodies, a 29k-triangle trimesh and 8 rays cost ~6 ms per step, so the sim runs ~170 steps/s with no renderer. That is why tests skip rendering (§15).\n\n### 2.7 AI Hub: what passes\n\nFetch once with `curl -fsSO` into `hub/`, from `https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/`: `session.js`, `harness.html`, `bridge.js`, `round.js`, `README.md`, `examples/arena.html`. Read the README: it is the contract. This skeleton passed every harness scenario with a heavy WebGPU scene in every copy (2 and 4 players on a poor network, host leaving, server copy):\n\n```js\nconst info = await AIHub.connect({ mode:'shared-world', seats:[1,4], card:true });\nif (!info) return startStandalone();             // not in a session: title screen, attract, everything\n// A session opens straight into the round: no title, menus or prompts other than the card.\naddEventListener('keydown', e => { if (e.key === 'Enter') AIHub.answer('ready'); });\nAIHub.on('card', c => drawCard(c));\nif (!info.server) startRendererInBackground();   // never block ready() on shaders; a server copy never renders\nbuildSimAndArena();\nAIHub.ready();                                   // once, no key press\nAIHub.on('start', () => unlockAudio());\nAIHub.on('message', (data, from) => net.receive(data, from));\nAIHub.on('leave', ({ id }) => sim.dropPlayer(id));\nAIHub.on('time-up', () => { if (AIHub.isHost) finishRound(); });   // at once, in the handler: graceMs is 5 s\nAIHub.on('end', ({ reason }) => endRound(reason));                  // stop input, sends and sound; hub shows results\nsetInterval(pumpSimAndNet, 50);                  // a timer, not rAF: four software-rendered copies crawl\n// Play begins when AIHub.time() >= 0; draw the countdown before that.\n```\n\nDetails that fail the check if missed:\n\n- The pasted client must be byte-exact and appear **once**. For client 1.4.0, SHA-256 from `/*! aihub-session ` through its last line (LF endings) is `529eac78c54cfff0e60d375a9c63f66d1a594327ddcc262a2bdf9b1f2fb6582a`. Never put the banner text anywhere else in the page.\n- Any `[AIHub]` console warning fails, so never exceed 20 sends/s (burst 40) or 16 KB. Keep your own token bucket at 18/s and keep unreliable messages under 1,100 bytes.\n- No `alert`, `confirm`, `prompt`, `window.open`, sockets, navigation or external `fetch`. Catch every promise (`requestPointerLock()`, `requestFullscreen()`, `playEffect()`, `audio.resume()`): an unhandled rejection counts as an error.\n- The harness pokes synthetic keys with `code:'w'`, not `KeyW`. Map by `e.code`, falling back to `e.key`.\n- On its own the game must draw and survive Enter/Space presses with no errors, and must leave `Math.random` alone. A DOM title over the canvas guarantees the \"drawn\" check even if WebGPU is unavailable.\n- In a session `localStorage` is an empty in-memory copy, so never depend on saved data there. Hub names are text: `textContent` only.\n- `Create + Options` belongs to the hub: ignore Options while Create is held.\n\nRun it like the hub does. Serve your dev folder from Node (`server.listen(0,'127.0.0.1')`), open with the five flags plus `--no-sandbox --autoplay-policy=no-user-gesture-required`, viewport 1280×860:\n\n```\n/hub/harness.html?game=/dist/game.html&players=N&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1&scenario=S&play=8000\n```\n\nWait for `body[data-complete=\"true\"]`, then require `window.__hubCheck.pass`. Scenarios: `players=2,3,4` with `standard`, `players=3` with `host-leave`, `players=2` with `server`. Each took 10–15 s here.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Architecture\n\n```\ntools/build.mjs  tools/test.mjs\nhub/             session client, harness (fetched, unedited)\ndocs/CONTENT.md  how to add a zone, enemy, weapon, item, script command (the designer's manual)\nSTATUS.md        your own progress notes, so a context reset costs nothing\nsrc/main.js      boot: session / standalone / test modes\nsrc/core/        loop, rng, events, tunables, save, coverage\nsrc/input/       action map, gamepad, keyboard+mouse, device tracking, virtual pads, bot injection\nsrc/phys/        Rapier wrapper: statics from pieces, character controllers, queries, ragdolls, debris\nsrc/sim/         player, weapons, damage, enemies + AI, nav, partner, director, inventory, shop, qte, script runner, triggers, bosses, siege, chapter flow\nsrc/content/     DATA ONLY: identity, weapons, items, enemies, shop stock, tunable defaults, zones/*, dialogue, documents, music patterns\nsrc/art/         palette, toon materials, prefab kit, character builder + outfits, weapon models, clip library, FX\nsrc/render/      renderer start, ink, light pool, camera rig, split screen, view sync\nsrc/audio/       engine and buses, reverb, sfx recipes, voice, music\nsrc/ui/          focus engine, glyphs, HUD, all screens, comic cutscene overlay\nsrc/net/         hub session flow, snapshot codec, rate limiter\nsrc/bot/         one brain shared by attract mode and the playthrough test\ntests/\n```\n\n**Sim and view are separate.** `src/sim` never touches the renderer, the DOM or audio. It owns state and may own CPU-only `Bone` hierarchies, because hit zones and mixers run there. It emits events on a bus; view, audio, UI and net subscribe. `?test=1&norender=1` runs the same code with no renderer at all, stepped by hand.\n\n**The sim is an object you can create and throw away,** with no module-level state: attract mode, retries and tests each make their own. On zone change call `world.free()` and dispose the old geometries and materials, so attract can loop for hours without running out of memory.\n\n**Loop.** Fixed 60 Hz:\n\n```js\nacc = min(acc + realDt * timeScale, 0.25); while (acc >= STEP) { sim.step(STEP); acc -= STEP; }\n```\n\n- `timeScale` handles hit-stop and slow motion by changing the step count; `dt` is never varied.\n- Rendering uses `renderer.setAnimationLoop`.\n- In a session a 50 ms `setInterval` also pumps the sim and net. A server copy has only the timer.\n- Standalone pauses on `visibilitychange`; sessions never pause.\n\n**Determinism.** All sim randomness comes from seeded streams in `core/rng.js` (from `AIHub.rng('siege')` in a session). `Math.random`, `Date.now` and `performance.now` are banned in `src/sim`, and a test greps for them. Visual-only randomness uses a separate cosmetic stream.\n\n**Tunables.** `tunables.define('enemy.hpMult', { label, min, max, step, def, group })`. Gameplay reads `T.enemy.hpMult` every time and never caches it, so dev sliders apply live. Defaults live in `src/content/tunables.js`.\n\n**Content is data.** So the rest of the game can be built later with ordinary tools, every zone, enemy, weapon, item, shop list, dialogue line and script is plain JSON-able data, documented in `docs/CONTENT.md`. A zone:\n\n```js\n{ id:'ch1.lane', title:'Hive Lane', palette:'dusk', music:'explore', reverb:'outdoor', size:[30,120],\n  terrain:{ seed:11, bumps:0.4, path:[[15,0],[14,60],[16,120]] },\n  pieces:[ {kit:'fence',at:[4,0,10],ry:0,len:30}, {kit:'farmhouse',at:[24,0,40],ry:-90,windows:['vault']} ],\n  lights:[ {kind:'lantern',at:[12,3,30]} ],\n  entry:{at:[15,0,2],ry:0}, exits:[ {to:'ch1.square',box:[10,0,118,20,3,120]} ],\n  spawns:[ {id:'e1',type:'sweetened',gear:'pitchfork',at:[14,0,40],wake:'seen'} ],\n  pickups:[ {item:'ammo9',n:15,at:[22,1,38],in:'crate'} ],\n  triggers:[ {box:[10,0,30,20,3,34],once:true,run:'ambush'} ],\n  scripts:{ ambush:[ ['say','dash','Friendly town.'], ['wake','e1'], ['music','tension'] ] },\n  bot:[ ['go',[15,50]], ['fight'], ['go',[15,118]] ] }\n```\n\nScript commands, the single language for level events and cutscenes: `say radio cam anim move wait wake spawn give flag if music sfx qte letterbox panel fade objective gate save chapterEnd`. Dev mode can copy the current zone as JSON and load a zone JSON dropped on the window.\n\n**Nav.** At zone load (after one `world.step()`), rasterise a 0.5 m walkable grid with down-rays and capsule overlap tests, with an 8-neighbour step-height check. `flowTo(target)` is a Dijkstra flow field, cached per target cell and refreshed at 4 Hz. Enemies, Winnie and the bot all use it, adding separation steering for crowds. Ladders, windows and gaps are explicit links that carry the action to play.\n\n**Hits.** Bullets ray-cast statics with `EXCLUDE_SENSORS` to get a stopping distance, then test ray against analytic capsules built from bone world positions (head sphere, torso, 2 arms, 2 legs). Deterministic, precise and independent of the renderer.\n\n**Test hook.** `window.__GAME`:\n\n- `state()`: mode, screen, chapter, zone, objective, cutscene, qte, focus, last device, player hp/ammo/weapon/pos, enemy count, partner, money, backend, `deviceLost`, `gpuErrors`, audio gains, coverage.\n- `step(n)` and `input(padState)`.\n- `teleport`, `setFlag`, `goZone`.\n\n---\n","numLines":135,"startLine":205,"totalLines":1149}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01E5C8MLtFKC25uFZEbLHFNL","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjEsPpr86jFBPPtqP4Fp","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_012cDG7nP8DjVsDFkwHBQmSi","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-215625__x13c81f/work/PLAN.md","offset":1005,"limit":120},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6605,"cache_read_input_tokens":329908,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6605},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9db0da04-284f-40b5-8e80-2e3f7ed2ab1c","uuid":"4d18b703-1214-4928-9b75-5c1a5804d695","timestamp":"2026-11-05T05:37:08.645Z","request_id":"req_011CgjEsPXFEHQoZ7RDNFKJb","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_012cDG7nP8DjVsDFkwHBQmSi":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-215625__x13c81f/work/PLAN.md","offset":1005,"limit":120}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012cDG7nP8DjVsDFkwHBQmSi","type":"tool_result","content":"1005\t## 14. Attract, Harvest Siege, multiplayer, dev mode\n1006\t\n1007\t### 14.1 Attract mode\n1008\t\n1009\t10 s with no input on any title or menu screen starts it. **Any** input (key, mouse move or click, pad button or stick, tap) exits at once back to the same menu.\n1010\t\n1011\t- It runs a sandboxed sim that never touches the save, driven by the bot through the same virtual pad a player uses, with god mode, infinite ammo and no-clip allowed.\n1012\t- Looping reel of about 90 s, 12–15 s per scene: Square brawl (kicks, slams) → Post Office siege and Harvester → Case and shop screens operating themselves → Effigy fire and climb → Gorge Wagon → Winnie stealth → Organ → Queen and launcher.\n1013\t- A corner stamp says DEMO and \"Press any button\" (glyph or key by last device).\n1014\t- Music follows the current scene at the normal bus level.\n1015\t\n1016\t### 14.2 Harvest Siege (arena mode)\n1017\t\n1018\tThe Festival Square at dusk. 5:00 clock, 1–4 players.\n1019\t\n1020\t- **Waves.** Every 40 s or when 5 or fewer remain; up to `16 + 6×players` alive; mix escalates Sweetened → Throwers → Keepers → Hiveheads; Harvester at 2:30 and 4:15.\n1021\t- **Score.** Kill 100 × chain (chain grows with kills within 6 s, up to ×8); headshot +50; kick or slam kill +150; Harvester 5,000.\n1022\t- **Mail Drops** parachute in every 45 s: Cross opens one for ammo plus a weapon, grenade or herb. Everyone starts with pistol, knife, 2 Yarrow.\n1023\t- **Down, not out.** A downed player crawls; a teammate holds Cross 2 s to revive. Solo gets one self-revive. All down ends the round.\n1024\t- **Standalone end screen:** rank stamp and a local top-5 table.\n1025\t\n1026\t### 14.3 Multiplayer\n1027\t\n1028\t**In an AI Hub session** (`AIHub.active`, protocol in `hub/README.md`, skeleton in §2.7):\n1029\t\n1030\tMode `shared-world`, seats `[1,4]`, the game's own card. The round is Harvest Siege, with no title screen, attract, saves or dev mode.\n1031\t\n1032\t- **Card** (`card:true`): the Square behind an ink wash, the game's name, each player in seat colour with a ready tick, how to win, this player's controls in the right glyphs, time left. Enter, Cross or a click answers Ready; Triangle, M or a click asks for More Time. No menus or choices; use `AIHub.rng('card')` for anything random.\n1033\t- **Authority.** The host (possibly a playerless `server` copy, which skips renderer, audio and input) runs the sim. Each copy moves its own player immediately and reports it.\n1034\t- **Traffic:**\n1035\t\n1036\t| Message | Direction | Reliable | Rate | Contents |\n1037\t|---|---|---|---|---|\n1038\t| `me` | client → host | no | 12 Hz | time, position, yaw, pitch, state, weapon |\n1039\t| `act` | client → host | yes | batched, ≤ 5 Hz | shots with hit claims `[enemyId, zone]`, kick, pickup, reload, revive |\n1040\t| `s` | host → all | no | 12 Hz | time, players, enemies as small int arrays; under 1,100 bytes (round-robin enemies across messages if more) |\n1041\t| `ev` | host → all | yes | batched, ≤ 5 Hz | spawn, death, drop, damage, explosion, score, wave, down, revive, over |\n1042\t\n1043\t- **Always talking.** `me` and `s` go out on schedule even when nothing moved: the check requires traffic both ways, and an idle player must still produce it.\n1044\t- **Hits.** The shooter's copy claims; the host checks the enemy is alive and within range + 2 m. Others are drawn 120 ms behind, interpolated. Late snapshots are dropped by `at`, as in `hub/examples/arena.html`.\n1045\t- **End.** On clock, all down or `time-up`, the host sends a final reliable `ev`, then `AIHub.finish({ standings, scores, stats, awards })`: standings by score over players still present, stats `{Kills, Headshots, Kicks}`. Awards under 24 characters: *Postmaster General* (top score), *Special Delivery* (most kicks), *Return to Sender* (most headshots). Omit `won` so individual ranks count.\n1046\t- **Leave:** drop the avatar. **`end`:** stop, show the reason, hub shows results.\n1047\t- **Pause:** Options opens a Settings-only overlay and the world keeps running. No Quit, Restart or Dev Mode.\n1048\t- Seat colours (`#e8443a #3b82f6 #22c55e #f5b700`) tint laser and armband. No chat, emotes or custom names.\n1049\t\n1050\t**On its own** (`AIHub.connect` gives `null`): the full game as designed, plus **couch co-op**, the natural multiplayer for a TV with no network or server. Harvest Siege → \"2 Players\": the second person presses Cross on another pad (first device stays P1; keyboard and mouse can be either). Split screen per §2.5, one HUD per player scaled to its half. Same sim, same rules, up to 2 players. Campaign is single-player. Add no other networking outside sessions; the About \"Online\" field says: AI Hub sessions only.\n1051\t\n1052\t### 14.4 Dev mode\n1053\t\n1054\tPause → Dev Mode. Same 10-foot screen, usable by pad, mouse or keys. Hidden in sessions.\n1055\t\n1056\t**Tools.** God mode, infinite ammo, no-clip fly camera, teleport (zone and mailbox list), chapter jump, skip cutscene, spawn enemy (type picker, at the laser dot), kill all, give any item, weapon or money, max upgrades, freeze AI, time scale. Overlays: colliders, hit zones, nav grid, triggers, spawners, vision cones. Toggles: ink, halftone. Stats: backend, frame time, enemy count. Test any QTE, voice line or music state. Copy position, copy zone JSON, load zone JSON (file drop), reset save, dump state.\n1057\t\n1058\t**Live sliders with a Reset to Defaults button** (each applies instantly, shows its value and default):\n1059\t\n1060\t| Group | Sliders |\n1061\t|---|---|\n1062\t| Player | Walk, sprint, aim shuffle speed, max HP, laser sway, recoil |\n1063\t| Combat | Head / leg / arm damage multipliers, crit chance, kick damage and radius, stagger thresholds, parry window, aim assist |\n1064\t| Enemies | HP multiplier, speed multiplier, damage multiplier, max attackers, token delay, windup time, spawn rate, Hivehead burst chance, Harvester speed |\n1065\t| Economy | Drop rate, ammo share, money multiplier, shop price multiplier |\n1066\t| Partner | Winnie HP, carry time, swat cooldown |\n1067\t| Feel | FOV, camera distance, hit-stop length, QTE window, siege wave interval, music level |\n1068\t\n1069\t---\n1070\t\n1071\t## 15. Testing\n1072\t\n1073\tTASK.md's rules apply: headless scripts first, screenshots only for what a script can't check, no subagents or workflows to debate, review, judge or audit. Keep one or two browsers open, close them after, keep files in your folder.\n1074\t\n1075\t**One command:** `npm test` (→ `tools/test.mjs`) prints only failures and a one-line count, e.g. `412 passed, 0 failed`. `npm test -- <group>` runs one group. Rerun a group only after changing the code it covers.\n1076\t\n1077\t**Fast sim.** Tests load `dist/game.html?test=1&norender=1&seed=7` and call `__GAME.step(n)` in a loop. Real-time rendering on SwiftShader is 1–3 fps, so never wait on it. Serve over `file://`, or Node on `listen(0,'127.0.0.1')` for the harness; confirm the page is yours before trusting a result. Stop only what you started.\n1078\t\n1079\t**The bot** (`src/bot/`). It reads the zone's `bot:` list, walks the flow field, aims at the nearest head, fires, reloads, kicks and slams on prompt, answers QTEs, operates levers, buys from a shopping list, and uses each boss's `botHint()`. Same brain as attract mode. A `--fair` run plays without cheats and may die; the coverage run uses god mode where needed.\n1080\t\n1081\t| Group | Checks |\n1082\t|---|---|\n1083\t| `lint` | No `TODO`, `FIXME`, `XXX`, `placeholder`, `stub`, `not implemented` in `src`. No `Math.random`, `Date.now`, `performance.now` in `src/sim`. No audio URLs or `new Audio(`. No banner text outside the client. No `alert`, `confirm`, `prompt`, `window.open` |\n1084\t| `build` | Single HTML, client hash matches, metas exact and in order, no network requests but the page itself, game title in `<title>` |\n1085\t| `sim` | Damage table, hit zones, stagger → kick → kill arithmetic, weapon stats and upgrades, case fitting and rotation, herb mixes, shop math, director drops, save/load round trip, tunables apply live, nav reaches every exit in every zone |\n1086\t| `playthrough` | The bot beats every chapter in order to the ending on seed 7, chapter by chapter so one can rerun alone. Coverage ids from it are recorded |\n1087\t| `ui` | Pad stub (`addInitScript` replacing `navigator.getGamepads` with a `mapping:'standard'` pad) and keyboard each walk every screen. Prompts flip with last device. Xbox glyph setting works. Focus never escapes. Hover moves focus. Case and shop by pad, mouse, keys. Create+Options ignored. No overflow at 1280×720 and 1920×1080 |\n1088\t| `modes` | Idle 10 s → attract; any input exits; it never writes the save. Touch-only (WebKit iPhone profile, `page.touchscreen.tap`) shows the message, Settings by tap, attract runs. Dev mode opens from pause; sliders change sim values; reset restores defaults. Couch co-op joins with two stub pads |\n1089\t| `render` | With the five flags: backend `webgpu`, no `deviceLost`, no `gpuErrors`, screenshot well above a blank page's size in each palette, warm-up covers all prefabs. No flags: backend `webgl2`, still drawing. Fails if more than 6 shadow lights exist |\n1090\t| `audio` | `OfflineAudioContext` renders of a gunshot, a voice line for each speaker and a bar of each music state are non-silent and unclipped. Voice length tracks text length. Music bus reads exactly 0.10 by default |\n1091\t| `hub` | All harness scenarios of §2.7 plus \"on its own\" (opens, Enter and Space, draws, no errors, `AIHub.active` false, `Math.random` untouched). No `[AIHub]` warnings |\n1092\t| `delivery` | Exit-interview file parses and matches TASK.md's shape, About screen shows all four sections with every Source Information field |\n1093\t\n1094\t**Coverage.** Across `sim`, `playthrough`, `ui` and `modes`, every id in §8.7 must be hit, or the run fails and names what's missing. A rare id like `crit` or `kill_harvester` may come from a `sim` scenario, but must be reachable in real play.\n1095\t\n1096\t**Eyes only for what scripts can't judge.** Screenshots at 1920×1080 of: title, HUD in each palette, case, shop, a crowd, each boss. Check silhouettes at thumbnail size (a stand-in for 10 feet). Fix what's muddy.\n1097\t\n1098\t---\n1099\t\n1100\t## 16. Build order\n1101\t\n1102\tEach milestone ends with its tests green, and a playable `dist/game.html`.\n1103\t\n1104\t| # | Milestone | Done when |\n1105\t|---|---|---|\n1106\t| M0 | **Skeleton.** Package, build, test runner, renderer with ink, sim loop, input, fonts, identity constant, hub client pasted, hub skeleton with a bare Square | `build`, `render`, `hub` groups green from day one |\n1107\t| M1 | **One person, one enemy.** Zone loader, kit builders with colliders, character builder and mixer, camera, aim, laser, pistol, one Sweetened, Crash Field blocked in | Bot walks and kills in `norender`; screenshot reads as the game |\n1108\t| M2 | **The loop.** Hit zones, staggers, kick, slam, knife, parry, nav, crowd tokens, director, FX, bursts, core SFX | A 15-enemy brawl feels right by the sim's numbers; `sim` group |\n1109\t| M3 | **The squeeze.** Focus engine, glyphs, HUD, case, items, herbs, shop, tuning, save, settings, pause | `ui` group for those screens |\n1110\t| M4 | **Chapter 1, whole.** Script runner, dialogue, voices, music, QTE, radio, comic panels, Lane, Square, Harvester, Post Office siege, results, game over, dev mode with all sliders, bot route | Bot finishes ch1; `audio` group; dev mode tests |\n1111\t| M5 | **Front end.** Title, attract, Field Manual, About, touch-only | `modes` group |\n1112\t| M6 | **Multiplayer.** Harvest Siege, session traffic, own card, couch co-op split | `hub` green with real gameplay; two stub pads play |\n1113\t| M7 | **Chapter 2.** Terraces, Keepers, Hiveheads, grenades, Test Range, mill puzzle, Effigy | Bot beats it |\n1114\t| M8 | **Chapter 3.** Winnie AI and commands, chapel, bell puzzle, Night Lane, Gorge Wagon | Bot beats it; partner ids hit |\n1115\t| M9 | **Chapter 4.** Monks, cannon, play-as-Winnie, Penitent, Wax and UV, Trent | Bot beats it |\n1116\t| M10 | **Chapter 5.** Organ with musical ranks, Queen, launcher, escape, ending, full attract reel | Full playthrough to credits; coverage complete |\n1117\t| M11 | **Finish.** Balance by `--fair` runs and sliders, 1080p eye pass, tips, documents, all feedback, About, exit interview, `--release` | Every test group green against the released file |\n1118\t\n1119\tDo M6 before the later chapters: it shapes the sim, and the hub check keeps a failing game out of sessions. Performance is out of scope per TASK.md: don't spend time on frame rate or optimisation. Spend it on detail, enemies, effects and lights (within §2.4's limit).\n1120\t\n1121\t---\n1122\t\n1123\t## 17. Delivery\n1124\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9db0da04-284f-40b5-8e80-2e3f7ed2ab1c","uuid":"a9d8a575-ae7c-47dc-8e4b-60c9aa764a74","timestamp":"2026-11-05T05:37:08.661Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-215625__x13c81f/work/PLAN.md","content":"## 14. Attract, Harvest Siege, multiplayer, dev mode\n\n### 14.1 Attract mode\n\n10 s with no input on any title or menu screen starts it. **Any** input (key, mouse move or click, pad button or stick, tap) exits at once back to the same menu.\n\n- It runs a sandboxed sim that never touches the save, driven by the bot through the same virtual pad a player uses, with god mode, infinite ammo and no-clip allowed.\n- Looping reel of about 90 s, 12–15 s per scene: Square brawl (kicks, slams) → Post Office siege and Harvester → Case and shop screens operating themselves → Effigy fire and climb → Gorge Wagon → Winnie stealth → Organ → Queen and launcher.\n- A corner stamp says DEMO and \"Press any button\" (glyph or key by last device).\n- Music follows the current scene at the normal bus level.\n\n### 14.2 Harvest Siege (arena mode)\n\nThe Festival Square at dusk. 5:00 clock, 1–4 players.\n\n- **Waves.** Every 40 s or when 5 or fewer remain; up to `16 + 6×players` alive; mix escalates Sweetened → Throwers → Keepers → Hiveheads; Harvester at 2:30 and 4:15.\n- **Score.** Kill 100 × chain (chain grows with kills within 6 s, up to ×8); headshot +50; kick or slam kill +150; Harvester 5,000.\n- **Mail Drops** parachute in every 45 s: Cross opens one for ammo plus a weapon, grenade or herb. Everyone starts with pistol, knife, 2 Yarrow.\n- **Down, not out.** A downed player crawls; a teammate holds Cross 2 s to revive. Solo gets one self-revive. All down ends the round.\n- **Standalone end screen:** rank stamp and a local top-5 table.\n\n### 14.3 Multiplayer\n\n**In an AI Hub session** (`AIHub.active`, protocol in `hub/README.md`, skeleton in §2.7):\n\nMode `shared-world`, seats `[1,4]`, the game's own card. The round is Harvest Siege, with no title screen, attract, saves or dev mode.\n\n- **Card** (`card:true`): the Square behind an ink wash, the game's name, each player in seat colour with a ready tick, how to win, this player's controls in the right glyphs, time left. Enter, Cross or a click answers Ready; Triangle, M or a click asks for More Time. No menus or choices; use `AIHub.rng('card')` for anything random.\n- **Authority.** The host (possibly a playerless `server` copy, which skips renderer, audio and input) runs the sim. Each copy moves its own player immediately and reports it.\n- **Traffic:**\n\n| Message | Direction | Reliable | Rate | Contents |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| `me` | client → host | no | 12 Hz | time, position, yaw, pitch, state, weapon |\n| `act` | client → host | yes | batched, ≤ 5 Hz | shots with hit claims `[enemyId, zone]`, kick, pickup, reload, revive |\n| `s` | host → all | no | 12 Hz | time, players, enemies as small int arrays; under 1,100 bytes (round-robin enemies across messages if more) |\n| `ev` | host → all | yes | batched, ≤ 5 Hz | spawn, death, drop, damage, explosion, score, wave, down, revive, over |\n\n- **Always talking.** `me` and `s` go out on schedule even when nothing moved: the check requires traffic both ways, and an idle player must still produce it.\n- **Hits.** The shooter's copy claims; the host checks the enemy is alive and within range + 2 m. Others are drawn 120 ms behind, interpolated. Late snapshots are dropped by `at`, as in `hub/examples/arena.html`.\n- **End.** On clock, all down or `time-up`, the host sends a final reliable `ev`, then `AIHub.finish({ standings, scores, stats, awards })`: standings by score over players still present, stats `{Kills, Headshots, Kicks}`. Awards under 24 characters: *Postmaster General* (top score), *Special Delivery* (most kicks), *Return to Sender* (most headshots). Omit `won` so individual ranks count.\n- **Leave:** drop the avatar. **`end`:** stop, show the reason, hub shows results.\n- **Pause:** Options opens a Settings-only overlay and the world keeps running. No Quit, Restart or Dev Mode.\n- Seat colours (`#e8443a #3b82f6 #22c55e #f5b700`) tint laser and armband. No chat, emotes or custom names.\n\n**On its own** (`AIHub.connect` gives `null`): the full game as designed, plus **couch co-op**, the natural multiplayer for a TV with no network or server. Harvest Siege → \"2 Players\": the second person presses Cross on another pad (first device stays P1; keyboard and mouse can be either). Split screen per §2.5, one HUD per player scaled to its half. Same sim, same rules, up to 2 players. Campaign is single-player. Add no other networking outside sessions; the About \"Online\" field says: AI Hub sessions only.\n\n### 14.4 Dev mode\n\nPause → Dev Mode. Same 10-foot screen, usable by pad, mouse or keys. Hidden in sessions.\n\n**Tools.** God mode, infinite ammo, no-clip fly camera, teleport (zone and mailbox list), chapter jump, skip cutscene, spawn enemy (type picker, at the laser dot), kill all, give any item, weapon or money, max upgrades, freeze AI, time scale. Overlays: colliders, hit zones, nav grid, triggers, spawners, vision cones. Toggles: ink, halftone. Stats: backend, frame time, enemy count. Test any QTE, voice line or music state. Copy position, copy zone JSON, load zone JSON (file drop), reset save, dump state.\n\n**Live sliders with a Reset to Defaults button** (each applies instantly, shows its value and default):\n\n| Group | Sliders |\n|---|---|\n| Player | Walk, sprint, aim shuffle speed, max HP, laser sway, recoil |\n| Combat | Head / leg / arm damage multipliers, crit chance, kick damage and radius, stagger thresholds, parry window, aim assist |\n| Enemies | HP multiplier, speed multiplier, damage multiplier, max attackers, token delay, windup time, spawn rate, Hivehead burst chance, Harvester speed |\n| Economy | Drop rate, ammo share, money multiplier, shop price multiplier |\n| Partner | Winnie HP, carry time, swat cooldown |\n| Feel | FOV, camera distance, hit-stop length, QTE window, siege wave interval, music level |\n\n---\n\n## 15. Testing\n\nTASK.md's rules apply: headless scripts first, screenshots only for what a script can't check, no subagents or workflows to debate, review, judge or audit. Keep one or two browsers open, close them after, keep files in your folder.\n\n**One command:** `npm test` (→ `tools/test.mjs`) prints only failures and a one-line count, e.g. `412 passed, 0 failed`. `npm test -- <group>` runs one group. Rerun a group only after changing the code it covers.\n\n**Fast sim.** Tests load `dist/game.html?test=1&norender=1&seed=7` and call `__GAME.step(n)` in a loop. Real-time rendering on SwiftShader is 1–3 fps, so never wait on it. Serve over `file://`, or Node on `listen(0,'127.0.0.1')` for the harness; confirm the page is yours before trusting a result. Stop only what you started.\n\n**The bot** (`src/bot/`). It reads the zone's `bot:` list, walks the flow field, aims at the nearest head, fires, reloads, kicks and slams on prompt, answers QTEs, operates levers, buys from a shopping list, and uses each boss's `botHint()`. Same brain as attract mode. A `--fair` run plays without cheats and may die; the coverage run uses god mode where needed.\n\n| Group | Checks |\n|---|---|\n| `lint` | No `TODO`, `FIXME`, `XXX`, `placeholder`, `stub`, `not implemented` in `src`. No `Math.random`, `Date.now`, `performance.now` in `src/sim`. No audio URLs or `new Audio(`. No banner text outside the client. No `alert`, `confirm`, `prompt`, `window.open` |\n| `build` | Single HTML, client hash matches, metas exact and in order, no network requests but the page itself, game title in `<title>` |\n| `sim` | Damage table, hit zones, stagger → kick → kill arithmetic, weapon stats and upgrades, case fitting and rotation, herb mixes, shop math, director drops, save/load round trip, tunables apply live, nav reaches every exit in every zone |\n| `playthrough` | The bot beats every chapter in order to the ending on seed 7, chapter by chapter so one can rerun alone. Coverage ids from it are recorded |\n| `ui` | Pad stub (`addInitScript` replacing `navigator.getGamepads` with a `mapping:'standard'` pad) and keyboard each walk every screen. Prompts flip with last device. Xbox glyph setting works. Focus never escapes. Hover moves focus. Case and shop by pad, mouse, keys. Create+Options ignored. No overflow at 1280×720 and 1920×1080 |\n| `modes` | Idle 10 s → attract; any input exits; it never writes the save. Touch-only (WebKit iPhone profile, `page.touchscreen.tap`) shows the message, Settings by tap, attract runs. Dev mode opens from pause; sliders change sim values; reset restores defaults. Couch co-op joins with two stub pads |\n| `render` | With the five flags: backend `webgpu`, no `deviceLost`, no `gpuErrors`, screenshot well above a blank page's size in each palette, warm-up covers all prefabs. No flags: backend `webgl2`, still drawing. Fails if more than 6 shadow lights exist |\n| `audio` | `OfflineAudioContext` renders of a gunshot, a voice line for each speaker and a bar of each music state are non-silent and unclipped. Voice length tracks text length. Music bus reads exactly 0.10 by default |\n| `hub` | All harness scenarios of §2.7 plus \"on its own\" (opens, Enter and Space, draws, no errors, `AIHub.active` false, `Math.random` untouched). No `[AIHub]` warnings |\n| `delivery` | Exit-interview file parses and matches TASK.md's shape, About screen shows all four sections with every Source Information field |\n\n**Coverage.** Across `sim`, `playthrough`, `ui` and `modes`, every id in §8.7 must be hit, or the run fails and names what's missing. A rare id like `crit` or `kill_harvester` may come from a `sim` scenario, but must be reachable in real play.\n\n**Eyes only for what scripts can't judge.** Screenshots at 1920×1080 of: title, HUD in each palette, case, shop, a crowd, each boss. Check silhouettes at thumbnail size (a stand-in for 10 feet). Fix what's muddy.\n\n---\n\n## 16. Build order\n\nEach milestone ends with its tests green, and a playable `dist/game.html`.\n\n| # | Milestone | Done when |\n|---|---|---|\n| M0 | **Skeleton.** Package, build, test runner, renderer with ink, sim loop, input, fonts, identity constant, hub client pasted, hub skeleton with a bare Square | `build`, `render`, `hub` groups green from day one |\n| M1 | **One person, one enemy.** Zone loader, kit builders with colliders, character builder and mixer, camera, aim, laser, pistol, one Sweetened, Crash Field blocked in | Bot walks and kills in `norender`; screenshot reads as the game |\n| M2 | **The loop.** Hit zones, staggers, kick, slam, knife, parry, nav, crowd tokens, director, FX, bursts, core SFX | A 15-enemy brawl feels right by the sim's numbers; `sim` group |\n| M3 | **The squeeze.** Focus engine, glyphs, HUD, case, items, herbs, shop, tuning, save, settings, pause | `ui` group for those screens |\n| M4 | **Chapter 1, whole.** Script runner, dialogue, voices, music, QTE, radio, comic panels, Lane, Square, Harvester, Post Office siege, results, game over, dev mode with all sliders, bot route | Bot finishes ch1; `audio` group; dev mode tests |\n| M5 | **Front end.** Title, attract, Field Manual, About, touch-only | `modes` group |\n| M6 | **Multiplayer.** Harvest Siege, session traffic, own card, couch co-op split | `hub` green with real gameplay; two stub pads play |\n| M7 | **Chapter 2.** Terraces, Keepers, Hiveheads, grenades, Test Range, mill puzzle, Effigy | Bot beats it |\n| M8 | **Chapter 3.** Winnie AI and commands, chapel, bell puzzle, Night Lane, Gorge Wagon | Bot beats it; partner ids hit |\n| M9 | **Chapter 4.** Monks, cannon, play-as-Winnie, Penitent, Wax and UV, Trent | Bot beats it |\n| M10 | **Chapter 5.** Organ with musical ranks, Queen, launcher, escape, ending, full attract reel | Full playthrough to credits; coverage complete |\n| M11 | **Finish.** Balance by `--fair` runs and sliders, 1080p eye pass, tips, documents, all feedback, About, exit interview, `--release` | Every test group green against the released file |\n\nDo M6 before the later chapters: it shapes the sim, and the hub check keeps a failing game out of sessions. Performance is out of scope per TASK.md: don't spend time on frame rate or optimisation. Spend it on detail, enemies, effects and lights (within §2.4's limit).\n\n---\n\n## 17. Delivery\n","numLines":120,"startLine":1005,"totalLines":1149}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_012cDG7nP8DjVsDFkwHBQmSi","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
