mbing, and screenshots stay blank. The five-flag list in the hub's own check script works. A smaller one: the hub repo's lib/kit targets three.js r186 and Rapier 0.20, which conflicts with the versions asked for unless you notice that the link points only at lib/hub.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"question\": \"What was the hardest thing to do?\",\n    \"answer\": \"Sizing the scope for builders I cannot see or answer. The brief asks for a complete demo showing every mechanic with no stubs, the source's appeal is constant variety, and the plan has to work in one run with no follow-up questions, whatever the builder's strength. Settling on 16 zones and 4 bosses, with the rule 'make it shorter, never thinner' and a feature list a test can enforce, took the most thought. Close behind was keeping how the source plays while making every name, character, level, line and look original.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"question\": \"What would you change in this prompt?\",\n    \"answer\": \"Put the five-flag WebGPU launch line in the 'This computer' section. Say in one sentence whether multiplayer is expected outside a hub session. Reword the art and animation lines for engines with no asset library or house style, for example 'build on the engine's own materials and animation system'. Link the raw hub README and say which client version is current. Tell the planner how capable the builders are and roughly how long the demo should play, because both decide the scope more than anything else in the brief.\"\n  }\n]\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null,"userModified":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01Krvv1HzggVhL44JsPCsEgW","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjEz43f7SB72t4d9GzkU","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01KTZVSgVQb2Raz1ecqQ3XdL","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"node - <<'EOF'\nconst fs = require('fs');\nconst plan = fs.readFileSync('PLAN.md', 'utf8');\nconst m = plan.match(/```js\\nimport \\* as THREE from 'three\\/webgpu';[\\s\\S]*?```/);\nconst printed = m[0].replace(/^```js\\n/, '').replace(/```$/, '').trim();\nconst tested = fs.readFileSync('_spike/src/ink.js', 'utf8').split('\\n').slice(1).join('\\n').trim();\nconsole.log('ink code identical to tested file:', printed === tested);\nconst banned = ['exit-interview.json', 'GameTitle', 'claude-opus', 'claude-haiku', 'Leon', 'Ashley', 'Salazar', 'Saddler', 'Krauser', 'Ada Wong', 'Ganado', 'Plaga', 'Mendez', 'Luis Sera', 'Hunnigan', \"What're ya\", 'Stranger', 'Pueblo', 'Regenerator', 'Garrador', 'El Gigante', 'Verdugo', 'TODO: ', '_spike', 'run2.mjs'];\nconst found = banned.filter((b) => plan.includes(b));\nconsole.log('banned strings found:', found.length ? found : 'none');\n// every section cross-reference points at a real heading\nconst heads = new Set([...plan.matchAll(/^#{2,3} (\\d+(?:\\.\\d+)?)\\./gm)].map((x) => x[1]).concat([...plan.matchAll(/^### (\\d+\\.\\d+) /gm)].map((x) => x[1])));\nconst refs = [...new Set([...plan.matchAll(/§(\\d+(?:\\.\\d+)?)/g)].map((x) => x[1]))];\nconsole.log('dangling refs:', refs.filter((r) => !heads.has(r)));\n// exit interview shape vs STAGE.md questions\nconst j = JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync('planner-exit-interview.json', 'utf8'));\nconst stage = fs.readFileSync('STAGE.md', 'utf8');\nconst qs = [...stage.matchAll(/^- (.+\\?)$/gm)].map((x) => x[1]);\nconsole.log('interview parses, entries', j.length, 'questions match STAGE.md in order:', JSON.stringify(j.map((e) => e.question)) === JSON.stringify(qs), 'keys ok:', j.every((e) => Object.keys(e).join() === 'question,answer'));\nconsole.log('plan words', plan.split(/\\s+/).length, 'KB', (plan.length / 1024).toFixed(1));\nEOF\necho ---; cat <<'EOF' | grep -c . \nplaceholder\nEOF\ngrep -n \"Title\\b\" PLAN.md | head -8; echo ---; du -sh _spike; ls _spike","description":"Final checks on plan, cross-references and interview file"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":16596,"cache_read_input_tokens":349336,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":16596},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9db0da04-284f-40b5-8e80-2e3f7ed2ab1c","uuid":"94f01e4c-8f51-49d3-b7e9-69b39c40ad8c","timestamp":"2026-11-05T05:38:50.917Z","request_id":"req_011CgjEz3ko4DpYDMJaJTR8f","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01KTZVSgVQb2Raz1ecqQ3XdL":{"command":"node - <<'EOF'\nconst fs = require('fs');\nconst plan = fs.readFileSync('PLAN.md', 'utf8');\nconst m = plan.match(/```js\\nimport \\* as THREE from 'three\\/webgpu';[\\s\\S]*?```/);\nconst printed = m[0].replace(/^```js\\n/, '').replace(/```$/, '').trim();\nconst tested = fs.readFileSync('_spike/src/ink.js', 'utf8').split('\\n').slice(1).join('\\n').trim();\nconsole.log('ink code identical to tested file:', printed === tested);\nconst banned = ['exit-interview.json', 'GameTitle', 'claude-opus', 'claude-haiku', 'Leon', 'Ashley', 'Salazar', 'Saddler', 'Krauser', 'Ada Wong', 'Ganado', 'Plaga', 'Mendez', 'Luis Sera', 'Hunnigan', \"What're ya\", 'Stranger', 'Pueblo', 'Regenerator', 'Garrador', 'El Gigante', 'Verdugo', 'TODO: ', '_spike', 'run2.mjs'];\nconst found = banned.filter((b) => plan.includes(b));\nconsole.log('banned strings found:', found.length ? found : 'none');\n// every section cross-reference points at a real heading\nconst heads = new Set([...plan.matchAll(/^#{2,3} (\\d+(?:\\.\\d+)?)\\./gm)].map((x) => x[1]).concat([...plan.matchAll(/^### (\\d+\\.\\d+) /gm)].map((x) => x[1])));\nconst refs = [...new Set([...plan.matchAll(/§(\\d+(?:\\.\\d+)?)/g)].map((x) => x[1]))];\nconsole.log('dangling refs:', refs.filter((r) => !heads.has(r)));\n// exit interview shape vs STAGE.md questions\nconst j = JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync('planner-exit-interview.json', 'utf8'));\nconst stage = fs.readFileSync('STAGE.md', 'utf8');\nconst qs = [...stage.matchAll(/^- (.+\\?)$/gm)].map((x) => x[1]);\nconsole.log('interview parses, entries', j.length, 'questions match STAGE.md in order:', JSON.stringify(j.map((e) => e.question)) === JSON.stringify(qs), 'keys ok:', j.every((e) => Object.keys(e).join() === 'question,answer'));\nconsole.log('plan words', plan.split(/\\s+/).length, 'KB', (plan.length / 1024).toFixed(1));\nEOF\necho ---; cat <<'EOF' | grep -c . \nplaceholder\nEOF\ngrep -n \"Title\\b\" PLAN.md | head -8; echo ---; du -sh _spike; ls _spike","description":"Final checks on plan, cross-references and interview file"}}}
